{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/408530-lashing-out-with-the-wolf","id":408530,"title":"Lashing out with the ... Wolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-16T20:01:37-08:00","id":408530,"title":"Lashing out with the ... Wolf?","content":"Okay, so I've been running Blood &amp; Smoke and there's indications there that werewolves have something that can be sensed by vampires and that might be able to lash out at them the same way they lash out with the Beast. Basically, for those who don't know B&amp;S, a vampire can focus their Beast to impact another creature (human, vampire, werewolf, whatever) and change their mood and urges. You can make a person competitive, easily tempted or trigger fight or flight in them. While, truthfully, I could just give werewolves the same ability to inflict such conditions, I'm tempted to give them something a little different but I don't know the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking some kind of Seduction condition that can temporarily cover for primal urge social penalties (tempting people to spend time with the Big Bad Wolf - perhaps akin to Swooning?), a Submission condition where the werewolf can basically use their essence like a force for dominance to compel a submissive demeanour (perhaps a condition where the target must spend willpower to make eye contact or stand up to the werewolf), and the Fight or Flight one still works as is.<br /> <br /> But yes, what do you guys think? It may not be the way the developers intend it, but it'd be a happy house rules in my game. Any thoughts? Suggestions on the mechanical backbone? Rotten fruit to fling at the idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:08:59-08:00","id":408549,"title":"","content":"I think its primal urge. Not sure how exactly it works so I may be wrong (need to re-read as im all apocalypse rules atm), but primal urge is their beast level, so it effects social rolls in much the same way, in apocalypse you rolled primal urge with charisma for sex magics. If you botched you terrified the shit out of the victim and they raaaaaaaaaan. Should note that in apocalypse primal urge is a talent and not... what it is in forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:36:26-08:00","id":408563,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/renown/\" target=\"_blank\">We've seen something like Lashing Out in the spoilers.</a> But until the book comes out using a version like you've mentioned seems like a good compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:03:43-08:00","id":408577,"title":"","content":"I don't think Primal Urge penalizes social rolls outright in this new iteration of the game. That may be reflected by your Harmony nowadays.<br /> <br /> Kindred lash their beast out, Forsaken flare their auspice nature. Cahalith being, for example Monstruous, and Rahu being, for instance Dominant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T04:44:09-08:00","id":408791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/408530-lashing-out-with-the-wolf?p=408563#post408563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/renown/\" target=\"_blank\">We've seen something like Lashing Out in the spoilers.</a> But until the book comes out using a version like you've mentioned seems like a good compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hunter's Aspects are indeed the 